te_hit_rate.py", "Experiments/RQ3/scripts/calculate_thresholds.py", "Experiments/RQ3/scripts/combined_dataset.jsonl", "Experiments/RQ3/scripts/local_with_scores.jsonl", "Experiments/RQ3/scripts/plot_fig.py", "Experiments/RQ3/scripts/run.sh", "Experiments/RQ3/scripts/split_data.py", "Experiments/RQ4/results/cem_mae_table.csv", "Experiments/RQ4/scripts/Baseline_CS.jsonl", "Experiments/RQ4/scripts/Baseline_sharecode.jsonl", "Experiments/RQ4/scripts/baseline_codescore_with_scores.jsonl", "Experiments/RQ4/scripts/baseline_sharecode_with_scores.jsonl", "Experiments/RQ4/scripts/create_table.py", "Experiments/RQ4/scripts/filter_to_analyze.py", "Experiments/RQ4/scripts/inference_on_CS.py", "Experiments/RQ4/scripts/inference_on_LoCaL.py", "Experiments/RQ4/scripts/inference_on_sharecode.py", "Experiments/RQ4/scripts/local_with_scores.jsonl", "Experiments/RQ4/scripts/run.sh", "Experiments/RQ4/scripts/worst100_by_metric/worst_top100_codebertscore.jsonl", "Experiments/RQ4/scripts/worst100_by_metric/worst_top100_codebleu.jsonl", "Experiments/RQ4/scripts/worst100_by_metric/worst_top100_codescore.jsonl", "Experiments/RQ4/scripts/worst100_by_metric/worst_top100_crystalbleu.jsonl", "Experiments/RQ5/results/mae_table_by_percent.csv", "Experiments/RQ5/scripts/Baseline.jsonl", "Experiments/RQ5/scripts/Local_test.jsonl", "Experiments/RQ5/scripts/calculate_MAE.py", "Experiments/RQ5/scripts/create_table.py", "Experiments/RQ5/scripts/inject_LoCaL_fixed.py", "Experiments/RQ5/scripts/mae_results.csv", "Experiments/RQ5/scripts/run.sh", "Experiments/RQ5/scripts/run_inference.py", "LICENSE", "Literature_Survey/get_stats.py", "Literature_Survey/metric_mentions.csv", "Literature_Survey/metrics_usage_filtered.csv", "Literature_Survey/query_sites.py", "LoCaL.jsonl", "README.md", "Source_Benchmarks/HE/HE_orig.jsonl", "Source_Benchmarks/MBPP/MBPP_orig.jsonl", "Source_Benchmarks/PIE/test.jsonl", "assets/scatter_plot.png", "assets/table_3.png", "assets/table_4.png", "assets/table_5.png", "assets/table_6.png", "requirements.txt"], "readme": "# LoCaL-Countering-Surface-Bias-in-CEMs\nThis repository contains the **replication package** and the **CEM evaluation benchmark, LoCaL**, introduced in the FSE 2026 paper:\n\n> ## LoCaL: Countering Surface Bias in Code Evaluation Metrics\n\n<br>\n\n**Note:** For consistency, figures and tables in this README use the same numbering as in the paper.\n\n---\n## :file_folder: Benchmark\n\nThe LoCaL benchmark is available at:\n\n```bash\n./LoCaL.jsonl\n```\n## :gear: Conda Environment\n1. Create a Conda env\n```bash\nconda create -n local python=3.8.20\n```\n2. Activate the environment\n```bash\nconda activate local\n```\n3. Install dependencies\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n## :bar_chart: Reproducing RQ1 results\n```bash\ncd Experiments/RQ1/scripts\nchmod +x run.sh\n./run.sh\n```\nThis will generate Table 3 inside the [`Experiments/RQ1/results`](Experiments/RQ1/results) directory.\n![Table 3 \u2014 RQ1 results](assets/table_3.png)\n\n## :bar_chart: Reproducing RQ2 results\n```bash\ncd Experiments/RQ2/scripts\nchmod +x run.sh\n./run.sh\n```\nThis will generate Table 4 inside the [`Experiments/RQ2/results`](Experiments/RQ2/results) directory.\n![Table 4 \u2014 RQ2 results](assets/table_4.png)\n\n## :bar_chart: Reproducing RQ3 results\n```bash\ncd Experiments/RQ3/scripts\nchmod +x run.sh\n./run.sh\n```\nThis will generate Figure 5 inside the [`Experiments/RQ3/results`](Experiments/RQ3/results) directory.\n![Figure 5 \u2014 RQ3_results](assets/scatter_plot.png)\n\n## :bar_chart: Reproducing RQ4 results\n```bash\ncd Experiments/RQ4/scripts\nchmod +x run.sh\n./run.sh\n```\nThis will generate Table 5 inside the [`Experiments/RQ4/results`](Experiments/RQ4/results) directory.\n![Table 5 \u2014 RQ4 results](assets/table_5.png)\n\n## :bar_chart: Reproducing RQ5 results\n1. Navigate to the scripts directory\n```bash\ncd Experiments/RQ5/scripts\n```\n2. Download trained models from [trained models](https://zenodo.org/records/17139161?preview=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzUxMiJ9.eyJpZCI6ImVlOTg3NjkzLTEwYzktNDYyMy1hNDQzLTA4ZmJkYTEwMjkzZiIsImRhdGEiOnt9LCJyYW5kb20iOiJjZjk5YTc0NTE1M2U0MDkyZGRkNWUwNmNiNmJjMzEyMiJ9.ybNeG0zu_Wv32PHgHQtwLl_HCuVevXiRwOS_ewEsFcXDNbxKUxaZFKK0hcePTxUww3Yc4eUTi8vXTSC026R93g)\n3. Follow the instructions in run.sh to generate results\n```bash\nchmod +x run.sh\n./run.sh\n```\nThis will generate Table 6 inside the [`Experiments/RQ5/results`](Experiments/RQ5/results) directory. <br>\n4. (Optional) To retrain the models \n  - Download the training and validation splits for each p(percentage of LoCaL) from [data_for_RQ5](https://zenodo.org/records/17139161?preview=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzUxMiJ9.eyJpZCI6ImVlOTg3NjkzLTEwYzktNDYyMy1hNDQzLTA4ZmJkYTEwMjkzZiIsImRhdGEiOnt9LCJyYW5kb20iOiJjZjk5YTc0NTE1M2U0MDkyZGRkNWUwNmNiNmJjMzEyMiJ9.ybNeG0zu_Wv32PHgHQtwLl_HCuVevXiRwOS_ewEsFcXDNbxKUxaZFKK0hcePTxUww3Yc4eUTi8vXTSC026R93g)\n  - Refer to the [CodeScore repository](https://github.com/Dingjz/CodeScore) for training instructions.\n\n![Table 6 \u2014 RQ5 results](assets/table_6.png)\n\n## :book: Literature Survey\n``` bash\npython3 get_stats.py\n```\n", "readme_present": true, "readme_scrub": {"leaked": false, "hits": {}}, "signals": {"dependency_manifest": ["requirements.txt"], "container": [], "build_script": [], "ci_config": [], "licence": ["LICENSE"], "tests": []}, "readme_referenced_paths": ["get_stats.py", "requirements.txt", "run.sh"], "pushed_at": "2026-04-20T23:45:01Z", "created_at": "2025-09-11T00:52:18Z", "stars": 0, "archived": false}